<title>USA: Robertson initiates E*Trade as &quot;buy&quot;.</title>
<headline>Robertson initiates E*Trade as &quot;buy&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robertson, Stephens &amp; Co said it had initiated coverage of electronic securities trading company E*Trade Group with a &quot;buy&quot; rating.</p>
<p>Robertson, Stephens analyst Cathy Baker said customer additions at E*Trade have averaged 10 percent a month, &quot;with strong client retention.&quot;</p>
<p>E*Trade provides consumers secure access to brokerage trading services via multiple gateways, including the Internet, on-line services, touch-tone phone and direct modem.</p>
<p>E*Trade shares closed up 3/8 at 9-1/8.</p>
<p>&quot;E*Trade continued strong growth and improved margins should drive the stock price to $15-18 in the next 12-18 months,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Silicon Valley Bureau, +1 415 846 5400</p>
